# CLI-deploy-only exclusions. Git-based deploys already respect .gitignore, but
# `vercel --prod` from the CLI walks the real filesystem before applying ignore
# rules — a pnpm monorepo's node_modules/.pnpm tree (tens of thousands of
# symlinked entries) is enough to crash that walk with "Array buffer allocation
# failed" even though every one of these paths is already gitignored and none
# of them are needed: Vercel's own remote build runs `pnpm install` itself.

node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
.turbo
test-results
playwright-report
apps/mobile/android
apps/mobile/ios
apps/extension/dist
apps/extension/*.zip
